I host headroom: RADIANCE_EXPERIMENTAL_CACHE_HEADROOM_BACKED: the RAM cache's slabs already hold 191.95 GiB of its 192.00 GiB budget, so the checks from here on keep 8.05 GiB free (--host-headroom-mib 8192 and the 56.00 MiB it has yet to grow) beside what they allocate
I chunk geometry: quantum 16 (attn block 16, state chunk 1), checkpoint interval 2048, max_tok 1024 -> prefill chunks of at most 1024
I prefix resume: exact -- a hit resumes only where an idle server's cold prefill of the same prompt starts a chunk (every 1024 tokens) and a prompt's tail snapshot is taken where its last chunk starts, so the hit recomputes the cold run's own chunks and answers bit-identically; a turn re-prefills up to one chunk more than --prefix-resume nearest
I checkpoint slots: auto: 7 linear-state + sliding-window snapshot(s) of 22.59 MiB in pinned host memory (158.16 MiB), none of it on the card; 7 a sequence for --max-num-seqs 1: geometric-backoff keeps 6 for a 32768-token session at a 2048-token interval, and one more for a running turn
I kv tiers: off (no --prefix-cache-mib); a finished conversation's KV stays in VRAM until the cache evicts it
